# Dialog and form theme

Dialogs, overlays, and form controls inside them follow the same `data-theme` tokens as the rest of Lámsza. Do not invent a second palette.

- Surfaces: `var(--card-bg)`, `var(--bg-body)`, `var(--border-color)`
- Text: `var(--text-primary)`, `var(--text-secondary)`, `var(--text-muted)`, `var(--text-faint)`
- Accents: existing brand tokens (`--szekely-red`, `--szekely-blue`, …)
- Inputs in `.link-dialog-form` already set background/color from tokens - nested widgets must too

```css
/* ❌ hard-coded light surface - unreadable in dark mode */
.item { background: #fff; color: #111; }

/* ✅ theme tokens */
.item {
  background: var(--bg-body);
  color: var(--text-primary);
  border: 1px solid var(--border-color);
}
```

Before finishing a dialog UI change, check both light and dark (`data-theme`). Selected chips, summary rows, helper text, and buttons must stay readable.
